  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It's great that VRChat lets you turn \"world volume\" down when necessary, but the fact is that different worlds have very different amounts (and intensities) of world audio; it would be more useful if VRChat just remembered your \"world volume\" setting for individual worlds that you visit (maybe the last 100 worlds you visited or whatever) and restored them on your next visit (and defaulted any new worlds to full volume, so people could at least hear what they're missing and turn it down if necessary).\n\nI know world creators can create a system like this manually with Udon, but most of them aren't going to bother, they'll just slap in some audio sources and let people adjust their world volume setting as necessary since that works fine...   but it feels silly as a user to have to re-adjust that adjustment every time you change worlds, when the client could just be remembering your preference.",
